{"parentUuid":"50acd9f8-1dd5-452a-831e-6261708d67e8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"gen_01KTQ050W5KQD13Q48T91WAXDT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. The title now appears immediately when navigating to the product page.\n\n**The problem:** `app/product/page.tsx` awaited `getInventory()` at the top of the page component, and that function calls `connection()`, which defers it to request time. With no Suspense boundary, Next.js couldn't send any of the page — even the static `<h1>Premium Widget</h1>` — until the inventory fetch finished, so navigation stalled on the slow data.\n\n**The fix:** I moved the fetch into a child `Inventory` component and wrapped it in `<Suspense>`. The title is now part of the prerendered static shell and shows up instantly on navigation, while the stock count and price stream in behind a \"Loading inventory...\" fallback.\n\nThe build confirms it: `/product` now reports as `◐ (Partial Prerender) — prerendered as static HTML with dynamic server-streamed content`, instead of fully dynamic."}],"model":"claude-fable-5","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5138,"cache_read_input_tokens":29911,"output_tokens":351,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5138},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"51b43a74-e8d4-4707-a7d1-16325aaa45f1","timestamp":"2026-06-09T20:11:10.476Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/workspace","sessionId":"0d8b1f30-d5e3-460b-a24d-72718aeec7a0","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"master"}
